# Music Notes - Development Guidelines

## Project Overview

This is a music notation web component library built with Lit. Components are designed to be used declaratively in HTML without requiring JavaScript knowledge from end users.

## Architecture Decisions

### Framework Choice: Lit
- Lightweight web components framework
- Uses decorators (`@customElement`, `@property`, `@state`) for reactive properties
- Shadow DOM for style encapsulation
- TypeScript for type safety

### Component Structure
- Each component is a self-contained custom element
- Components communicate via attributes and CSS custom properties
- Slotted content allows composition (e.g., notes inside measures, measures inside staff)

## Technical Decisions

### Pitch Positioning System
- Treble clef positions defined in `TREBLE_CLEF_POSITIONS` mapping
- E4 = position 0 (bottom staff line), B4 = position 4 (middle line)
- Each position step = 4px vertical offset (half of 8px line spacing)
- Notes use `transform: translateY()` for positioning to avoid layout recalculation

### Stem Direction Logic
- Individual notes: stems up if below B4, stems down if on/above B4
- Beamed groups: use average pitch of all notes to determine uniform direction
- Threshold: position >= 4 means stems down

### Ledger Lines
- Automatically rendered for notes outside staff range
- Below staff: C4 (position -2) and lower need ledger lines at even positions
- Above staff: A5 (position 10) and higher need ledger lines at even positions
- Ledger lines centered on note head (12px wide note head, 18px wide ledger line)

### Beaming Implementation
- `<music-beam>` wraps notes to be beamed together
- Sets `beamed` and `stem-down` attributes on child notes
- Beam position calculated from stem element bounding rectangles
- Uses CSS custom properties (`--beam-left`, `--beam-width`, `--beam-top`) for positioning

### Timing for Beam Calculation
- Must wait for notes to re-render after setting stem direction
- Uses nested `requestAnimationFrame` calls:
  1. First frame: set attributes on notes
  2. Second frame: calculate beam position after notes have re-rendered

## Known Limitations

### CSS Anchor Positioning
- Investigated using CSS Anchor Positioning for beam placement
- **Does not work across Shadow DOM boundaries**
- Anchors defined in one shadow root cannot be referenced from another
- Current solution: hybrid approach with minimal JS for position calculation

### Beam Positioning for Different Pitches
- For ascending/descending note groups, beam connects at extremes:
  - Stems up: beam at highest stem top (minimum Y)
  - Stems down: beam at lowest stem bottom (maximum Y)
- Currently uses `getBoundingClientRect()` for accurate positioning

## CSS Custom Properties

### Theming
- `--note-color`: Color for notes, stems, beams (default: #000)
- `--beam-thickness`: Beam line thickness (default: 4px)
- `--line-spacing`: Staff line spacing (default: 8px)

### Internal Communication
- `--hide-flags`: Set by music-beam to hide flags on beamed notes

## File Structure

```
src/components/
├── index.ts          # Exports all components
├── music-note.ts     # Note rendering with pitch positioning
├── music-rest.ts     # Rest symbols
├── music-measure.ts  # Measure container with bar lines
├── music-staff.ts    # Staff lines container
├── music-beam.ts     # Beam grouping for eighth/sixteenth notes
├── music-meter.ts    # Time signature
├── music-tempo.ts    # Tempo marking
└── music-dynamics.ts # Dynamic markings (pp, p, mp, mf, f, ff)
```

## Common Patterns

### Adding New Pitch Range
Update `TREBLE_CLEF_POSITIONS` in both:
- `src/components/music-note.ts`
- `src/components/music-beam.ts`

### Debugging Beam Issues
- Console logging is available in `calculateBeamPosition()`
- Check: stem direction, stem bounding rects, calculated beam position
- Verify notes have re-rendered before calculating (timing issue)

## Testing Considerations

- Test notes at various pitches (within staff, above, below)
- Test beamed groups with same pitch and different pitches
- Test ascending and descending note patterns
- Verify ledger lines appear correctly for out-of-staff notes
- Test components both inside `<music-staff>` and standalone (legend)

